<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hongkou</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hongkou is a district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shanghai">Shanghai</a> north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suzhou">Suzhou</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscogee">Creek</a>. An American settlement was established there in 1848 and merged with the British settlement in 1863 to form the International Settlement. In the early 20th century it housed a large Japanese community, and during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> the Japanese confined Jewish refugees from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> to a ghetto in the district.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hongkou.jpg" alt="Hongkou" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 冰纪 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_North_Bund,_Hong_Kou,_SHANGHAI.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
